WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.760
“I have an announcement to make
about wrongdoing at Waystar Royco.”

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.680
The Season Two finale of Succession
ends with Brian Cox’s titan of

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.840
industry, Logan Roy, cracking a
small, barely perceptible smile.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.360
It’s a smile that might seem odd
given that he’s watching his son,

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.800
Kendall, publicly throw him under
the bus on TV and expose his

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.320
culpability for the cruises scandal
that could cause him to be ousted

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.800
as CEO from the company he built.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.600
“I have with me today
copies of records

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.680
that show his personal sign-off…”

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.800
But I think this is the
day his reign ends.”

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.840
So why does Logan look, on some level,
a little bit happy about this?

